Well, the answer is, yes, sort of, but not really. First of all, you
should avoid using arrows unless they are +2 or more and blessed and
you have maxed luck. Otherwise they get mulched (in the beginning, use
the +2 one mostly, since they get mulched less often, but only for
emergencies). Once you do mines end and can bless your starting +2
arrows, you can use the bow more often. (I also donate to any
coaligned unicorn whenever I see one). And once you get the longbow,
just a few thousand turns of frequent #invokes plus you current stock
should get you a nice supply. (Note: +2 blessed and lucky works in
3.4.3 for sure, but not in 3.4.1, not sure about 3.4.2).


Now, the main question is whether it's worthwile for a ranger to use a
bow. AFAICT, daggers will always do more damage than equally enchanted
arrows, since they get the strength bonus. Elves or orcs firing their
racial arrows from their racial bow get an extra shot (extra .5 on
average) but you'll be hard-pressed to find enough of those to
enchant, and you can't rely on the reflection from the longbow. I
looked at Slashem, and there an enchanted bow gets you extra shots,
which makes bow worthwile (though there is a bug where any enchanted
weapon gets you extra shots of any projectile). They also have another
artifact bow which gets +7 damage per arrow but I've never tried it,
and looks way overpowered.

The nice thing about arrows is that you can carry hundreds of them
with you, say, 100 or 200 in a bag of holding and 50 in main
inventory, which allows you to clear out a midsized zoo or throne room
without having to stop to recover daggers getting yourself in danger.
Just break down the door, step back and start shooting.

So it becomes a playstyle thing mostly. The little extra damage from
daggers versus the ability to just keep shooting. Plus role-playing I
guess.  (Oh, and arrows can be poisoned). I choose the extra ammo, but
that's just me.

Personally, I think the longbow should at least give you an extra shot
or +2 damage, or something else to make arrows worthwhile. The bonus
to hit is basically negligible, since rangers will need to keep their
luck maxed anyway.

(On a side note, now that using enchanted arrows is feasible, maybe it
makes sense to change the artifact spoiler to include the +0 longbow
of diana using +7 arrows in the damage table).


